; ★★ AND THE BIT POSITIONS ARE AN ORDER, not just a set of names. The
; reference's own comment above this block: *the numeric values of TypeFlags
; determine the order computed by the CompareTypes function and therefore the
; order of constituent types in union types* — so this table decides how a
; union PRINTS, which is what the fifth yardstick compares. Generating it is
; how that order stays the reference's.
;
